a)	Conditional Blocks
Aim: To use IF, IF-ELSIF and CASE statements in PL/SQL.
Theory: PL/SQL provides IF-THEN-ELSE, IF-THEN-ELSIF for range checks, simple CASE for equality tests on one value, and searched CASE for arbitrary conditions. CASE can also be used as an expression.



Program 1.1: IF-ELSIF (grade by salary)

DECLARE
  v_sal  emp.sal%TYPE;
  v_name emp.ename%TYPE;
BEGIN
  SELECT ename, sal INTO v_name, v_sal FROM emp WHERE empno = 102;

  IF v_sal >= 30000 THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(v_name || ': Grade A');
  ELSIF v_sal >= 10000 THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(v_name || ': Grade B');
  ELSE
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(v_name || ': Grade C');
  END IF;
END;
